The connecting maps are explicit. For a first-opening object `K_open` with
root vertex `r`, endpoint vertices `p_h`, and object-fiber Hermitian lines
`L_r,L_pM,L_pQ,L_pG`, let

```text
E_open(K_open;L)
  = L_r direct-sum
    direct-sum_(h in {M,Q,G}) L_p_h
```

be the endpoint-alternative carrier. The direct-sum decomposition defines the
canonical summand injection

```text
iota_open:E_open(K_open;L)->C_0(K_open;L).
```

It is the identity on each displayed object fiber and zero on all other
vertex summands. No basis vector or metric normalization is chosen here. The
unresolved preparation is the projective root ray `P(L_r)`. Only after Gate 3
derives the counting Hermitian forms may `iota_open` be called an isometry and
may a unit representative of that ray be used. Applying the
handle-forgetful functor removes the endpoint labels after the injection; it
does not identify the four alternatives.

The complete cell-counting Hilbert carrier is

```text
H_cell(K)=C_0(K;L) direct-sum C_1(K;L) direct-sum C_2(K),
```

while the primitive odd incidence operator acts on the invariant subcarrier

```text
H_BID(K)=C_0(K;L) direct-sum C_1(K;L).
```

`C_2` supplies the counting metric and generated face-response carrier; it is
not silently included in the primitive `B_D` orbit. Accordingly, the
projective state orbit used below lies in `P(H_BID)`.

Finally, the real face-flux cochains and complex face carrier are connected by
the canonical real-form map

```text
c_2:A_R^2(K)->C_2(K),
c_2(sum_f a_f f)=sum_f a_f |f>,

A_R^2(K) tensor_R C ~= C_2(K).
```

No identification is made between connection tangents `A_R^1`, chain states
`C_1`, or endpoint alternatives; every later use must display its map.